1
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:16,216
PREVIOUSLY

2
00:00:16,282 --> 00:00:19,352
-KARINA and WINTER of aespa!
-It's great to see you!

3
00:00:19,419 --> 00:00:21,287
Yes, I plan to go very far today.

4
00:00:21,354 --> 00:00:23,156
I hope our episodes are the funniest.

5
00:00:23,423 --> 00:00:24,758
THAT'S AESPA'S SPIRIT

6
00:00:24,824 --> 00:00:26,092
I can rotate my hand 360 degrees.

7
00:00:26,159 --> 00:00:27,927
-What?
-What was that?

8
00:00:28,261 --> 00:00:29,996
THE SEAL CLAP PARTY TRICK

9
00:00:30,230 --> 00:00:31,898
WHY IS AESPA TRYING SO HARD?

10
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:35,168
We invited their right-hand men

11
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:36,836
and put together a new kind of team round.

12
00:00:36,903 --> 00:00:39,205
Hello, I am head chef Kim Seon-yeop,
who's been working

13
00:00:39,272 --> 00:00:40,607
with Chef Hyun-suk for 14 years.

14
00:00:40,673 --> 00:00:43,209
I am Woo Do-hee,
and I work at L'Amant Secret.

15
00:00:43,276 --> 00:00:44,744
What's one weakness that he has?

16
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:47,013
He tends to fish for praise.

17
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:47,914
He fishes for compliments.

18
00:00:47,981 --> 00:00:49,949
I thought I'd end up
only cleaning up after him.

19
00:00:50,016 --> 00:00:51,384
It's a rare sight to see him shy.

20
00:00:51,451 --> 00:00:53,686
I got secondhand embarrassment
watching him.

21
00:00:53,753 --> 00:00:54,687
Yes, I'm sure.

22
00:00:54,754 --> 00:00:56,389
I'm looking forward to today.

23
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:57,791
AND

24
00:00:57,857 --> 00:00:59,659
For the first time in the show's history,

25
00:00:59,726 --> 00:01:01,361
they'll play with their right-hand men.

26
00:01:01,428 --> 00:01:03,430
It's exhilarating
when teamwork is perfect.

27
00:01:03,496 --> 00:01:05,865
<i>-It's in 30-second intervals.</i>
<i>-Thirty seconds?</i>

28
00:01:05,932 --> 00:01:07,267
-Grind the black pepper.
-Yes, Chef.

29
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:08,768
-Did you add lemon juice?
-I did.

30
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:10,136
LIKE THEIR ACTUAL KITCHEN

31
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:12,772
PERFECT DETAILS

32
00:01:12,839 --> 00:01:14,374
The teamwork of 14 years.

33
00:01:14,441 --> 00:01:15,575
Where's the sugar, Seon-yeop?

34
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:16,743
Seon-yeop, lemon juice.

35
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:18,144
Is he cleaning up after him?

36
00:01:18,211 --> 00:01:19,946
-Salt!
-Whoa!

37
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:21,347
SALT CROSS

38
00:01:21,614 --> 00:01:22,982
THE TEAMWORK THEY'VE BUILT
FOR THE PAST 14 YEARS

39
00:01:23,049 --> 00:01:25,185
So you have to be this good
to be fine dining chefs.

40
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:26,419
WHAT DO THEY TASTE LIKE?

41
00:01:26,486 --> 00:01:28,054
-It's good.
-It's good.

42
00:01:28,121 --> 00:01:30,056
-It's so tough to choose.
-It's getting harder.

43
00:01:30,123 --> 00:01:31,758
This is KARINA's choice.

44
00:01:32,025 --> 00:01:34,828
WHAT'S THE RESULT
OF THE FIRST ASSISTED TEAM ROUND?

45
00:01:34,894 --> 00:01:39,199
You're watching <i>Chef & My Fridge</i>
with KARINA and WINTER of aespa.

46
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:42,502
Actually, we owe
a portion of our show to aespa.

47
00:01:42,569 --> 00:01:44,737
-Have you watched us?
-So often.

48
00:01:44,804 --> 00:01:48,141
-It's often trending on Reels.
-Is that so?

49
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:50,410
-He uses our songs the most often.
-Right.

50
00:01:50,477 --> 00:01:52,679
You're facing this way today.

51
00:01:52,745 --> 00:01:55,648
-I want to see them.
-It's as if we're facing each other.

52
00:01:55,715 --> 00:01:56,850
He won't look at me.

53
00:01:58,384 --> 00:01:59,552
ALL I NEED IS AESPA

54
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:00,553
All right.

55
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,689
-Some even say that…
-He's so silly.

56
00:02:02,755 --> 00:02:05,625
…Ho-young has done the dance
more often than aespa themselves.

57
00:02:05,692 --> 00:02:07,994
Even at the ceremonial first pitch.

58
00:02:08,061 --> 00:02:11,231
Yes, I did the dance first
before pitching.

59
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:12,732
You did "su-su-su-supernova"?

60
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,100
Even at overseas events,

61
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,503
they'd have "Supernova" ready to play.

62
00:02:16,569 --> 00:02:17,637
MUST DANCE EVEN WHEN ABROAD

63
00:02:17,704 --> 00:02:20,240
They ask me to do the dance
before I actually get to work.

64
00:02:20,306 --> 00:02:21,674
KARINA said,

65
00:02:21,741 --> 00:02:23,810
as she watched him dance,

66
00:02:23,877 --> 00:02:27,213
she felt a sense of familiarity
and sympathized with him.

67
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,248
Did you say this?

68
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:29,883
-Familiar?
-She felt he was familiar?

69
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:31,484
-With Ho-young.
-Me?

70
00:02:31,551 --> 00:02:33,319
KARINA felt she was similar to him.

71
00:02:33,386 --> 00:02:35,021
My arms are on the shorter end…

72
00:02:35,088 --> 00:02:36,256
-Yes.
-…compared to my height.

73
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:38,791
-Really?
-I keep them folded, so not many know,

74
00:02:38,858 --> 00:02:40,527
but they're short compared to my height,

75
00:02:40,593 --> 00:02:43,696
and so, I'm good at recognizing
someone with short arms.

76
00:02:43,763 --> 00:02:45,632
KARINA SYMPATHIZED WITH HIM

77
00:02:45,698 --> 00:02:47,133
They are short.

78
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:50,136
-You probably notice them more often.
-They are short.

79
00:02:50,203 --> 00:02:51,571
I don't think his arms are short.

80
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:54,207
I think his torso ate into his arms.

81
00:02:54,274 --> 00:02:55,108
As he got bigger.

82
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,543
Yes, his torso began to expand.

83
00:02:56,609 --> 00:02:58,912
-It got hungry.
-It ate into the arms.

84
00:02:58,978 --> 00:03:01,347
Were you always aware of that
since you were young?

85
00:03:01,414 --> 00:03:02,782
I didn't know,

86
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:04,684
but until middle school,
I was nicknamed T-Rex.

87
00:03:04,751 --> 00:03:06,186
-What?
-What?

88
00:03:06,252 --> 00:03:07,420
THE SHORT-ARMED DINOSAUR…

89
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:08,955
The dinosaur with these arms?

90
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:11,558
-Karinasaur.
-I'd always go, "They aren't that short."

91
00:03:11,624 --> 00:03:14,494
But one day, I compared my arms
with the shortest girl in my class,

92
00:03:14,561 --> 00:03:16,296
-and my arms were shorter.
-What?

93
00:03:16,362 --> 00:03:18,565
I'm 168 cm tall,

94
00:03:18,631 --> 00:03:19,933
and she was in the 140 cm range.

95
00:03:19,999 --> 00:03:20,934
In the 140 cm range?

96
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,404
When you spread out like this,
she'll have less space here.

97
00:03:25,171 --> 00:03:27,640
-They aren't that short!
-They aren't that short.

98
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:29,542
I'm sorry.

99
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,544
ADDICTED TO THE SEAL CLAP

100
00:03:31,611 --> 00:03:33,546
So there's something

101
00:03:33,613 --> 00:03:36,716
-KARINA wants to say to Eun-yeong.
-To me?

102
00:03:36,783 --> 00:03:37,984
EXCITED

103
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:41,221
She says,
"Don't be mean to Ho-young and Sung-jun."

104
00:03:41,287 --> 00:03:42,355
-Right.
-Seriously.

105
00:03:42,422 --> 00:03:44,457
-She's mean.
-He has short limbs.

106
00:03:44,524 --> 00:03:46,693
-She says they have short limbs.
-He has short limbs.

107
00:03:46,759 --> 00:03:49,662
It's the word "limbs."

108
00:03:49,729 --> 00:03:51,130
-Right.
-The word itself?

109
00:03:51,598 --> 00:03:52,999
TRIGGERED

110
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,867
-It was triggering.
-It hurts.

111
00:03:55,235 --> 00:03:56,502
SELF-REFLECTION

112
00:03:56,569 --> 00:03:58,705
I'm sure you've made efforts
to overcome that characteristic.

113
00:03:58,771 --> 00:04:00,340
-I cover them up.
-Covering them up.

114
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,309
LIKE THIS?

115
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:04,544
HAIR TOO SHORT

116
00:04:04,611 --> 00:04:06,946
-Use your hair.
-To divert attention from my arms.

117
00:04:07,013 --> 00:04:09,682
-That's why I'm quick with my steps.
-Yes.

118
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:12,685
We'd like to offer Ho-young
a special opportunity.

119
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:15,421
-Would you like to dance with her?
-Together?

120
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:16,723
Yes, with KARINA.

121
00:04:17,156 --> 00:04:19,359
GETS UP IMMEDIATELY

122
00:04:20,059 --> 00:04:22,195
KARINA X JUNG HO-YOUNG'S DANCE!

123
00:04:22,695 --> 00:04:24,430
It's an honor.

124
00:04:24,497 --> 00:04:26,266
THE HONOR IS MINE

125
00:04:26,332 --> 00:04:28,434
-What now?
-Make sure you learn from her.

126
00:04:28,501 --> 00:04:30,136
The ratio difference is uncanny.

127
00:04:31,471 --> 00:04:33,406
THE DIFFERENCE IS SO EVIDENT…

128
00:04:34,307 --> 00:04:35,742
THE SUPER UDON IS ON ITS WAY!

129
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:37,377
Ready, go.

130
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:39,746
<i>Su-Su-Su-Super Udon</i>

131
00:04:40,113 --> 00:04:41,848
HER UPPER BODY MOVES WITH THE LEGS

132
00:04:42,915 --> 00:04:44,217
ONLY MOVING THE UPPER BODY

133
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:45,585
She's moving the legs too.

134
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:47,353
-Move your legs.
-Your legs are still.

135
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:49,289
-He's…
-Whoa!

136
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:50,823
OOH, AHH

137
00:04:51,224 --> 00:04:53,760
HIS TEACHER GIVES HIM A LESSON

138
00:04:53,826 --> 00:04:55,762
HIS LEGS FINALLY BEGIN TO MOVE

139
00:04:55,828 --> 00:04:58,131
-We only focused on the arms.
-We did!

140
00:04:58,364 --> 00:04:59,866
AFTER THE LESSON, ONE MORE TIME

141
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:02,302
DIVERTING ATTENTION

142
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:05,071
FULLY CHARGED WITH CONFIDENCE

143
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,707
His dancing looks much better now.

144
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:09,375
-That was different.
-It was better.

145
00:05:09,442 --> 00:05:11,477
-Now I know the real dance.
-Yes.

146
00:05:11,544 --> 00:05:13,613
It's much better
now that our attention is diverted.

147
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,814
A TIP FOR THE SHORT-ARMED

148
00:05:14,881 --> 00:05:18,217
-The key was moving the legs.
-It was much better with the legs.

149
00:05:18,284 --> 00:05:19,319
All right.

150
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:21,487
We received a tip.

151
00:05:21,554 --> 00:05:23,623
As of this taping,

152
00:05:23,690 --> 00:05:27,694
KARINA is about to challenge herself
to something big tomorrow.

153
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,195
It's literally her D-day.

154
00:05:29,262 --> 00:05:31,397
-Yes, it's important.
-What's this about?

155
00:05:31,464 --> 00:05:32,899
Tomorrow, I have

156
00:05:32,965 --> 00:05:34,400
my driver's license test.

157
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:36,202
Driver's license test?

158
00:05:36,269 --> 00:05:37,470
Tomorrow is the test?

159
00:05:37,537 --> 00:05:40,006
-The on-road driving exam.
-The on-road? She must be nervous.

160
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:41,708
-You did the course?
-The driving course test

161
00:05:41,774 --> 00:05:43,810
ended with full marks.

162
00:05:44,444 --> 00:05:45,511
I KNEW IT

163
00:05:45,578 --> 00:05:47,347
Are you licensed to drive?

164
00:05:47,413 --> 00:05:50,817
This is the first time I'm sharing this,

165
00:05:50,883 --> 00:05:51,884
but yes, I am.

166
00:05:51,951 --> 00:05:53,152
-Whoa.
-Really?

167
00:05:53,219 --> 00:05:54,487
-You passed.
-I did.

168
00:05:54,554 --> 00:05:56,889
Let's cheer for KARINA
so that she'll pass with one try.

169
00:05:56,956 --> 00:05:58,358
OH MY

170
00:05:58,591 --> 00:06:00,259
WE HOPE YOU PASS THE DRIVING TEST

171
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:03,296
You might as well
show up in person to show support.

172
00:06:03,363 --> 00:06:05,598
I'm about to show up at the office.

173
00:06:05,665 --> 00:06:07,400
You can go, "KARINA! You got this!"

174
00:06:07,467 --> 00:06:09,135
-Huh? What's this?
-Hey, wait.

175
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:12,138
Unlike us, there's someone
who's against you getting

176
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,974
-your driver's license?
-Someone's against this?

177
00:06:15,041 --> 00:06:18,244
-So your father is adamantly against this?
-Your father?

178
00:06:18,311 --> 00:06:21,314
I don't want to sound like
I'm trying to make my dad sound great,

179
00:06:21,381 --> 00:06:23,549
but he said, "It's my joy
to pick you up when you call."

180
00:06:23,783 --> 00:06:25,184
THE DAD WITH A DAUGHTER CAN RELATE

181
00:06:25,518 --> 00:06:27,954
BLUSH

182
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,856
-He must love picking her up.
-He said I won't need it.

183
00:06:29,922 --> 00:06:32,392
He's such a doting father,

184
00:06:32,458 --> 00:06:35,161
and he always sends flower baskets
whenever I hold concerts

185
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:38,831
with the sweetest messages attached.

186
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:40,066
When I go on a tour,

187
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:42,702
he'd mark my whereabouts on the map.

188
00:06:42,769 --> 00:06:44,137
MARKING HER WHEREABOUTS ON THE MAP

189
00:06:44,203 --> 00:06:46,739
-That's why he's against it.
-He's very sweet.

190
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:49,909
You know, her sweet father
with all these stories

191
00:06:49,976 --> 00:06:53,312
once served in the Marine Corps.

192
00:06:53,379 --> 00:06:55,014
So within the Marine Corps,

193
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:56,883
aespa and KARINA were famous

194
00:06:56,949 --> 00:07:00,219
even before they made their debut.

195
00:07:00,286 --> 00:07:01,487
We have proof, so let's see it.

196
00:07:01,554 --> 00:07:03,489
-Oh, please don't.
-Whoa. What is it?

197
00:07:04,056 --> 00:07:05,892
There it is.

198
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:08,761
It's the Marine Corps
social media account.

199
00:07:09,061 --> 00:07:10,963
FAINTS

200
00:07:11,030 --> 00:07:12,999
-"Yu Cheol's daughter is"…
-His daughter.

201
00:07:13,065 --> 00:07:14,967
-…"debuting as a girl group."
-Yu Cheol's daughter.

202
00:07:15,034 --> 00:07:18,638
"We're proud of her
overcoming many days as a trainee."

203
00:07:18,704 --> 00:07:21,908
"Yu Ji-min was a member of aespa,
debuting as KARINA."

204
00:07:21,974 --> 00:07:23,776
-It drives me nuts.
-She was posted

205
00:07:23,843 --> 00:07:26,145
on the Marine Corps social media account.

206
00:07:26,212 --> 00:07:28,815
-Is that the official account?
-It's the official one.

207
00:07:28,881 --> 00:07:30,049
It's the official account.

208
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,484
-You're big among the Marines.
-Yes.

209
00:07:31,551 --> 00:07:33,052
I'm huge.

210
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:34,320
BLUSH

211
00:07:34,987 --> 00:07:37,890
It feels really weird
to see my dad's name here.

212
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:40,026
-Yu Cheol's daughter.
-Yu Cheol's daughter.

213
00:07:40,092 --> 00:07:41,494
Yu Cheol.

214
00:07:41,561 --> 00:07:45,097
She's a beloved daughter
with a doting father at home,

215
00:07:45,164 --> 00:07:48,901
but she's also aespa's leader.

216
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:50,903
Has your personality changed
during your career?

217
00:07:51,838 --> 00:07:53,639
I'm the youngest at home,

218
00:07:53,706 --> 00:07:57,310
so I used to be the cutesy type.

219
00:07:57,376 --> 00:07:59,445
But our members are all avoidant types.

220
00:07:59,512 --> 00:08:01,380
The other three?

221
00:08:01,447 --> 00:08:02,648
Including me.

222
00:08:02,715 --> 00:08:04,050
All four of you?

223
00:08:04,116 --> 00:08:06,085
When we have to make a decision,

224
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,554
we always go, "She'll do it."

225
00:08:08,621 --> 00:08:10,256
So you put it on each other.

226
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:12,058
So I have to go,
"Is it yes or no? Tell me,

227
00:08:12,124 --> 00:08:13,226
or we're not going home."

228
00:08:13,759 --> 00:08:15,895
THE LEADER HAS BECOME RESOLUTE

229
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:18,598
-Has your personality changed over time?
-It definitely did.

230
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:21,534
Speaking of, let's ask Chef Seon-yeop

231
00:08:21,601 --> 00:08:23,402
what Hyun-suk is like as a leader.

232
00:08:23,469 --> 00:08:25,505
Yes, his own leader.

233
00:08:25,571 --> 00:08:26,706
CURIOUS

234
00:08:26,772 --> 00:08:29,709
-He's a type who sets an example.
-He sets an example?

235
00:08:29,775 --> 00:08:31,177
How does he set an example?

236
00:08:31,244 --> 00:08:32,945
The motto of our restaurant

237
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,847
is to let our customers leave

238
00:08:34,914 --> 00:08:38,384
with the feeling that
they have watched a fun comedy film.

239
00:08:38,451 --> 00:08:39,752
That's our motto.

240
00:08:39,819 --> 00:08:41,153
When he walks out,

241
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:44,056
-he asks me to get him some salt.
-Right.

242
00:08:44,123 --> 00:08:47,126
-He asks for some salt in his hand…
-Right.

243
00:08:47,193 --> 00:08:50,630
-…to do a tour around the tables.
-A round.

244
00:08:50,696 --> 00:08:52,431
Does he go around with salt in his hand?

245
00:08:52,999 --> 00:08:55,134
I have to give it to him in a small dish.

246
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:58,137
So he's pretty much
the restaurant's clown!

247
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:00,139
"Let the clown in!"

248
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,541
And he comes in with salt, "Yessir!"

249
00:09:01,607 --> 00:09:03,476
YOU LITTLE…

250
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:04,877
It's like hand-pulled noodles.

251
00:09:04,944 --> 00:09:06,679
-You're right.
-Like at those hot pot places.

252
00:09:06,746 --> 00:09:09,181
-He's performing like the noodle guy.
-A performance.

253
00:09:09,382 --> 00:09:11,450
CHEF & MY FRIDGE HAS HYUN-SUK'S SALT

254
00:09:11,517 --> 00:09:13,986
I actually like my food bland

255
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:15,621
but you can make mine salty.

256
00:09:17,290 --> 00:09:18,124
GOTCHA

257
00:09:18,357 --> 00:09:19,592
GIGGLING

258
00:09:19,926 --> 00:09:21,360
GOT MY RESPECT…

259
00:09:21,427 --> 00:09:22,962
It'll be drenched in salt.

260
00:09:23,029 --> 00:09:27,333
Chef Jong-won, what kind of leader
do you think you are?

261
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:30,336
There are many younger people in my team,

262
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:31,437
so I try not to be stuck up.

263
00:09:31,504 --> 00:09:34,974
I believe
I'm not the stuck-up kind of leader.

264
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:37,743
I try to understand their language too,
like abbreviations.

265
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:38,811
Like <i>yareu</i>?

266
00:09:38,878 --> 00:09:41,147
-The dishes today are <i>yareu</i>.
-It's so <i>yareu</i>.

267
00:09:41,213 --> 00:09:43,583
She hates that slang.

268
00:09:43,649 --> 00:09:45,251
You don't like <i>yareu</i>?

269
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:46,452
What does it mean?

270
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:48,854
-When people feel great. <i>Yareu</i>.
<i>-Yareu</i>.

271
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:51,057
-Geez.
-Back in my day, it was "Oh, <i>yareu</i>."

272
00:09:51,123 --> 00:09:52,692
Why do you hate it?

273
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,694
It's just the word itself, it's…

274
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,228
-Sounds shallow?
-Yes!

275
00:09:56,295 --> 00:09:57,396
Hey, KARINA. <i>Yareu</i>.

276
00:09:57,797 --> 00:09:59,231
SHUDDERING

277
00:09:59,298 --> 00:10:00,299
WINTER, <i>yareu</i>.

278
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:02,168
GIGGLING

279
00:10:02,234 --> 00:10:04,337
aespa is here today, <i>yareu</i>!
So you don't like that?

280
00:10:04,403 --> 00:10:06,072
-<i>Yareu</i>.
-<i>Yareu</i>.

281
00:10:06,138 --> 00:10:09,208
He's definitely not the stuck-up type.

282
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:10,843
-But does he think so?
-Right?

283
00:10:10,910 --> 00:10:12,178
We have a transcript.

284
00:10:12,244 --> 00:10:14,380
-A transcript?
-I knew this would come up.

285
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:15,581
I knew it.

286
00:10:15,648 --> 00:10:17,116
Do-hee talked about team dinners,

287
00:10:17,183 --> 00:10:20,953
-and he seems to have a different opinion.
-What did he say?

288
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:23,222
"There's too much pressure
on our team dinners."

289
00:10:24,323 --> 00:10:25,791
What's the reason?

290
00:10:25,858 --> 00:10:27,226
EYES WIDENED

291
00:10:27,293 --> 00:10:30,296
-But he's so nice to you.
-I knew this was the case.

292
00:10:30,363 --> 00:10:32,331
-Do you force him to drink?
-It's never forced.

293
00:10:32,398 --> 00:10:34,667
-Then why is there so much pressure?
-Right?

294
00:10:34,734 --> 00:10:36,936
He never forces us
to come to team dinners,

295
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:41,474
but it's because he's always serious
whenever he does something.

296
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:44,043
For example, when we go bowling,

297
00:10:44,110 --> 00:10:47,680
-there's pressure when I'm on his team.
-I get it.

298
00:10:47,747 --> 00:10:48,981
Does he have to win?

299
00:10:49,048 --> 00:10:50,082
He has to win.

300
00:10:50,316 --> 00:10:51,951
EVERYONE SIGHS

301
00:10:52,018 --> 00:10:54,086
Team dinners are supposed to be fun.

302
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:55,388
I wouldn't go.

303
00:10:55,688 --> 00:10:57,356
JUST FINDS IT HILARIOUS

304
00:10:57,423 --> 00:11:00,259
Chef Do-hee also shared with us
that even for team dinners,

305
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,495
Jong-won has to plan everything out.

306
00:11:02,561 --> 00:11:03,796
Are you serious?

307
00:11:03,863 --> 00:11:05,564
-How tiring.
-In five-minute intervals?

308
00:11:05,631 --> 00:11:07,700
It's to produce some fun.

309
00:11:07,767 --> 00:11:10,936
-Because it has to be fun.
-He just mentioned one of them.

310
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:12,538
What about a toast? Do you make those?

311
00:11:12,605 --> 00:11:14,040
We do that too.

312
00:11:14,106 --> 00:11:16,342
I heard you have to make
an acrostic poem with his name.

313
00:11:16,409 --> 00:11:19,211
He has to make an acrostic poem
with Jong-won's name for the toast?

314
00:11:19,278 --> 00:11:21,580
-I've seen it.
-With your name?

315
00:11:21,647 --> 00:11:23,315
Do you have to do
card stunt performances too?

316
00:11:23,382 --> 00:11:26,085
-With cards.
-Yes, with colored cards.

317
00:11:26,152 --> 00:11:28,521
-Son! Jong! Won!
-Jong! Won!

318
00:11:28,587 --> 00:11:29,755
-The best!
-The best!

319
00:11:30,056 --> 00:11:31,857
SON JONG-WON, KNOCKED OUT

320
00:11:31,924 --> 00:11:33,759
-Right?
-I guess he does that.

321
00:11:33,826 --> 00:11:35,127
Even for team dinners,

322
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:38,364
I want to do something
that isn't too cliché,

323
00:11:38,431 --> 00:11:40,933
so I try my best to let them have fun.

324
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,535
I didn't know he took it like this.

325
00:11:42,601 --> 00:11:43,703
JOKING

326
00:11:43,769 --> 00:11:46,238
-He wanted to make it different.
-Yes.

327
00:11:46,305 --> 00:11:48,240
It's completely different from ours.

328
00:11:48,307 --> 00:11:51,110
-What do you do?
-For us… He should be talking, actually.

329
00:11:51,177 --> 00:11:53,345
-Tell us.
-I just pay the tab

330
00:11:53,412 --> 00:11:55,581
and give them my credit card
to go karaoke or something.

331
00:11:55,648 --> 00:11:57,983
I do that to let them relax and have fun.

332
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,585
It must've taken lots of self-control

333
00:11:59,652 --> 00:12:00,720
for him not to go karaokeing.

334
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:02,555
How bad would he have wanted to go!

335
00:12:02,621 --> 00:12:04,457
It's incredible. Give him a hand!

336
00:12:04,657 --> 00:12:05,825
YOU'RE INCREDIBLE, CHOI HYUN-SUK

337
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:08,928
This guy who loves to sing
doesn't follow them to the karaoke room?

338
00:12:09,662 --> 00:12:10,730
FEELING PROUD

339
00:12:10,796 --> 00:12:13,599
And now, following WINTER's fridge
in the previous episode,

340
00:12:13,666 --> 00:12:16,802
we're about to look
through KARINA's fridge.

341
00:12:16,869 --> 00:12:18,838
Feel free to use
the shelf-stable ingredients.

342
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:23,943
And let me make a note
that these bottles here are KARINA's.

343
00:12:24,009 --> 00:12:25,678
Do you have more alcohol inside?

344
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,613
-They're only out here.
-Only out here?

345
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,814
Quite the true drinker.

346
00:12:30,216 --> 00:12:32,118
Those who do not drink their alcohol cold

347
00:12:32,184 --> 00:12:34,653
-are truly those who love to drink.
-Is that so?

348
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,355
WINTER has a long way to go.

349
00:12:36,422 --> 00:12:38,023
She specializes
in drinking from the bottle.

350
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:40,493
STRAIGHT FROM THE BOTTLE

351
00:12:40,893 --> 00:12:42,428
SHE'S DEFINITELY NUMBER 1 IN THAT AREA…

352
00:12:42,995 --> 00:12:45,698
EMBARRASSED

353
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:47,633
-Let's take a look at her fridge.
-Okay.

354
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:49,935
-I'm nervous.
-Let's look through her fridge.

355
00:12:50,002 --> 00:12:52,271
We present KARINA's fridge!

356
00:12:53,672 --> 00:12:57,543
AMAZED

357
00:12:57,777 --> 00:13:00,146
PRESENTING KARINA'S FRIDGE

358
00:13:02,648 --> 00:13:03,649
There are lots, right?

359
00:13:03,716 --> 00:13:07,353
-Even WINTER looks surprised.
-That's a lot.

360
00:13:07,419 --> 00:13:08,387
What's that?

361
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:10,189
It's <i>yareu</i>.

362
00:13:10,756 --> 00:13:12,158
Ugh!

363
00:13:12,224 --> 00:13:13,526
Look at the top two shelves.

364
00:13:13,592 --> 00:13:15,795
The first and the second shelves

365
00:13:15,861 --> 00:13:17,229
-have so many side dishes.
-That's a lot.

366
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,898
Who made all these for you?

367
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:23,302
They're all from my aunt,
my mom's older sister.

368
00:13:23,369 --> 00:13:26,005
My mom is currently abroad
to study another language.

369
00:13:26,405 --> 00:13:27,306
AMAZED

370
00:13:27,373 --> 00:13:30,576
So my aunt made those side dishes
instead of my mom.

371
00:13:32,244 --> 00:13:34,013
You must be so grateful.

372
00:13:34,079 --> 00:13:36,148
-Do you prefer Korean food?
-Absolutely.

373
00:13:36,215 --> 00:13:38,017
She says she loves Korean food.

374
00:13:38,083 --> 00:13:40,252
-It's a lot, right?
-These are all Korean side dishes.

375
00:13:40,319 --> 00:13:41,520
I probably have lots of kimchi.

376
00:13:41,587 --> 00:13:43,088
-You do.
-She does have a lot.

377
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:44,323
The second shelf is all kimchi.

378
00:13:44,390 --> 00:13:45,758
It's almost like a kimchi fridge.

379
00:13:45,825 --> 00:13:47,560
ALMOST LIKE A KIMCHI FRIDGE

380
00:13:47,626 --> 00:13:50,863
-You've already had a lot.
-Yes, she has already had some.

381
00:13:50,930 --> 00:13:53,399
-Yes.
-She had lots. Look at how empty it is.

382
00:13:53,966 --> 00:13:55,868
Look. It does look delicious.

383
00:13:55,935 --> 00:13:58,137
-It's really good.
-Is it <i>kkakdugi</i>?

384
00:13:58,204 --> 00:14:00,105
-Young radish kimchi.
-It already looks great.

385
00:14:00,172 --> 00:14:02,474
-Perfect with <i>ramyeon</i>.
-It's so good.

386
00:14:02,541 --> 00:14:05,277
You can already tell right here
that she's a Korean food person.

387
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,946
But why is she named KARINA?

388
00:14:07,012 --> 00:14:09,248
HIS REMARK WAS SO YAREU

389
00:14:09,315 --> 00:14:12,351
She's KARINA
because she likes beer with her kimchi.

390
00:14:12,418 --> 00:14:14,553
-Whoa.
-KARINA, bring some Corona.

391
00:14:14,887 --> 00:14:16,856
OH…

392
00:14:17,122 --> 00:14:18,190
EVEN THE GRANDPA'S MAD

393
00:14:18,757 --> 00:14:19,658
That was so corny.

394
00:14:19,725 --> 00:14:21,927
HIS COMMENT WAS SO CORNY

395
00:14:21,994 --> 00:14:23,762
You don't dislike Western food, right?

396
00:14:23,829 --> 00:14:26,198
No, but I can't make anything,

397
00:14:26,265 --> 00:14:28,567
so I usually go out
to eat Western cuisine.

398
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:30,302
POTATO, SPINACH, CELERY, ZUCCHINI…

399
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:31,971
We're going to see lots of stuff.

400
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:34,974
She has some fruit
on the third shelf, including watermelon.

401
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,343
-What are these? Kiwis?
-Kiwis.

402
00:14:37,409 --> 00:14:39,011
-It's a lot.
-They aren't ordinary kiwis,

403
00:14:39,078 --> 00:14:40,746
but ruby kiwis.

404
00:14:40,813 --> 00:14:42,281
-What now?
-Ruby kiwis.

405
00:14:42,348 --> 00:14:45,017
-It's red inside, right?
-Yes.

406
00:14:45,084 --> 00:14:48,354
When it's cut in half,
it's ruby-red on the inside.

407
00:14:48,420 --> 00:14:49,722
And it's much sweeter.

408
00:14:49,788 --> 00:14:51,390
SOUNDS DELICIOUS

409
00:14:51,457 --> 00:14:53,592
I'm allergic to kiwis,

410
00:14:53,659 --> 00:14:54,493
but I still eat them.

411
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:55,828
-Because it's good?
-Allergic?

412
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,863
-You just eat it?
-You put up with it?

413
00:14:57,930 --> 00:15:00,299
-Yes, I just scratch myself later.
-Scratch yourself?

414
00:15:00,366 --> 00:15:02,768
-Try some. It's really good.
-It's really good.

415
00:15:02,835 --> 00:15:04,904
-It's really good?
-It is.

416
00:15:05,337 --> 00:15:06,272
CHOP

417
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:09,475
-So there's the color.
-Isn't it pretty?

418
00:15:09,541 --> 00:15:11,243
IT'S REALLY RUBY-RED

419
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,212
You can get it out like this.

420
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:15,247
POPS OUT

421
00:15:16,015 --> 00:15:17,650
YUM

422
00:15:22,955 --> 00:15:24,823
He ate the sticker.

423
00:15:25,190 --> 00:15:27,559
HE EVEN ATE THE STICKER

424
00:15:28,794 --> 00:15:30,462
PTOOEY…

425
00:15:30,529 --> 00:15:32,798
-It's good.
-Yes, it's good.

426
00:15:32,865 --> 00:15:34,833
PROUD

427
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,268
KARINA, I hear you're the type

428
00:15:36,335 --> 00:15:39,805
who puts on weight quickly
and sheds it quickly too.

429
00:15:39,872 --> 00:15:41,607
My weight fluctuates a lot.

430
00:15:41,674 --> 00:15:44,176
-I've gained 4 kg in one day…
-In a day?

431
00:15:44,243 --> 00:15:46,278
-…and I've shed it on the same day.
-Did she say 4 kg?

432
00:15:46,345 --> 00:15:47,446
Is that possible?

433
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:48,747
But how?

434
00:15:48,814 --> 00:15:50,549
It was back when I was a trainee.

435
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:53,185
That day, I stuffed myself
with everything I wanted,

436
00:15:53,252 --> 00:15:55,421
felt so full, and tapped on my belly.

437
00:15:55,487 --> 00:15:58,324
I knew it was trouble, so I weighed myself
and saw I had gained 4 kg.

438
00:15:58,590 --> 00:15:59,992
IN TOTAL SHOCK

439
00:16:00,059 --> 00:16:02,061
The next day was our weigh-in day,

440
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:04,997
so I turned up the heater
in the practice room,

441
00:16:05,064 --> 00:16:08,200
put on leggings, a sweat suit,
a zip-up hoodie on top

442
00:16:08,267 --> 00:16:09,401
and a padded jacket.

443
00:16:09,468 --> 00:16:10,469
A padded jacket?

444
00:16:10,536 --> 00:16:14,606
Yes, and we played the top 100 chart
and ran around together.

445
00:16:14,673 --> 00:16:18,043
After that, I went home
and did an hour of lower-body bathing.

446
00:16:18,110 --> 00:16:21,046
When I did that,
I was completely drenched in sweat.

447
00:16:21,113 --> 00:16:22,748
-You dried yourself out.
-I did.

448
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:25,184
I hear UFC fighters do that.

449
00:16:25,250 --> 00:16:26,585
And you dropped 4 kg?

450
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:28,220
But now,

451
00:16:28,287 --> 00:16:29,855
I'm too old

452
00:16:29,922 --> 00:16:32,224
to eat or work out like that.

453
00:16:32,291 --> 00:16:34,259
-Because she's too old?
-Do you feel

454
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:36,628
that you've become a bit older?

455
00:16:36,695 --> 00:16:39,365
Recently, very much.

456
00:16:39,431 --> 00:16:40,699
I'm in pain when it rains.

457
00:16:40,899 --> 00:16:41,734
LOL

458
00:16:42,634 --> 00:16:43,936
She's in pain when it rains?

459
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,938
-Yes, it aches when it rains.
-Because you're older?

460
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,773
We have a guy who went through the famine.

461
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,775
THE GRANDPA
IS SERIOUSLY IN PAIN IN THE RAIN

462
00:16:49,842 --> 00:16:50,709
He's even used a pack carrier.

463
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:52,778
A pack carrier?

464
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,114
I guess people don't use those anymore.

465
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,316
Let's look at the freezer.

466
00:16:57,383 --> 00:17:00,386
Frozen cocktail shrimp.

467
00:17:00,452 --> 00:17:01,587
Mackerel.

468
00:17:01,653 --> 00:17:04,423
-What's in here? Meat.
-Meat.

469
00:17:04,490 --> 00:17:06,091
-I probably have a lot.
-Yes, meat.

470
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:09,361
Yes, and you have many different cuts.
You have lots of meat.

471
00:17:09,428 --> 00:17:11,030
I really love meat.

472
00:17:11,096 --> 00:17:13,532
What if you can only have
one cut of meat right now?

473
00:17:14,733 --> 00:17:16,702
THAT'S SO HARD TO CHOOSE…

474
00:17:17,469 --> 00:17:18,537
Can't she just have a whole pig?

475
00:17:18,604 --> 00:17:20,072
MAKE IT EASIER

476
00:17:20,139 --> 00:17:21,907
ONE WHOLE PIG

477
00:17:21,974 --> 00:17:25,044
-My all-time favorite is pork belly.
-Pork belly.

478
00:17:25,110 --> 00:17:26,078
I love it.

479
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:28,313
I can have it all week long
and not get sick of it.

480
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:32,718
She could've been nicknamed T-Rex
because she likes meat so much.

481
00:17:32,785 --> 00:17:35,020
-A carnivore?
-Yes, because it's a carnivore.

482
00:17:35,087 --> 00:17:36,188
She loves meat a lot.

483
00:17:36,755 --> 00:17:39,191
That's all for KARINA's fridge!

484
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:41,527
FINISHED CHECKING OUT KARINA'S FRIDGE

485
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:45,397
What kind of orders
does she have today for the chefs?

486
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:47,833
Show us her orders!

487
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:50,102
What does she want to order?

488
00:17:50,169 --> 00:17:52,838
I Woke Up
and Found Myself in Cooking Comics.

489
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:54,873
-That sounds hard.
-Right.

490
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:56,642
What do you mean by this?

491
00:17:56,708 --> 00:18:00,712
-I love to read comics…
-Right.

492
00:18:00,779 --> 00:18:03,115
…so I want to eat something that's good

493
00:18:03,182 --> 00:18:05,317
but also looks like
something from a comic book.

494
00:18:05,384 --> 00:18:06,985
-Special.
-Something special.

495
00:18:07,052 --> 00:18:10,489
I wanted to put that order in
because I wanted to get

496
00:18:10,556 --> 00:18:14,293
a dish that makes me feel like
I'm reading a comic book.

497
00:18:14,359 --> 00:18:16,195
So it needs to look creative.

498
00:18:16,261 --> 00:18:18,197
-Yes, I hope so.
-This one

499
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:21,033
-is advantageous for Poong.
-You're right.

500
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:23,168
THAT'S TRUE

501
00:18:23,235 --> 00:18:25,304
You should join the round.

502
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:27,339
-Think about it.
-We'll see.

503
00:18:27,406 --> 00:18:29,007
-After seeing the second one.
-Let me see it.

504
00:18:29,074 --> 00:18:31,643
-I don't think Hyun-suk will pick it.
-Right.

505
00:18:31,710 --> 00:18:34,379
When he wakes up,
he's like, "I'm glad I'm still alive."

506
00:18:36,381 --> 00:18:37,883
What are you trying to say?

507
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:39,918
When he wakes up, he goes, "I'm alive."

508
00:18:39,985 --> 00:18:42,454
You aren't much younger than I am.

509
00:18:42,754 --> 00:18:44,256
ALSO IN HIS 50S, BUT DRAWS THE LINE

510
00:18:44,323 --> 00:18:46,191
-"I'm alive today."
-"I'm still alive."

511
00:18:46,758 --> 00:18:47,759
All right.

512
00:18:47,826 --> 00:18:51,063
Now, what's the second order
KARINA has brought?

513
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:53,465
-Lemonade.
-That one

514
00:18:53,532 --> 00:18:54,867
-is a part of your lyrics.
-Yes.

515
00:18:54,933 --> 00:18:56,635
It's actually "I'll make it LEMONADE."

516
00:18:57,903 --> 00:19:00,139
So please make me lemonade

517
00:19:00,205 --> 00:19:03,976
and a dish
that'll go well with the beverage.

518
00:19:04,042 --> 00:19:05,711
I thought I'd ask.

519
00:19:05,777 --> 00:19:06,979
Food pairing.

520
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:10,883
-She used a part of the lyrics.
-That's right.

521
00:19:10,949 --> 00:19:12,417
The fight has already been set,

522
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:14,920
because these two
will have to play as teams.

523
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:18,790
Chef Hyun-suk and Jong-won
must join the same round.

524
00:19:18,857 --> 00:19:20,359
Yes, join the same round.

525
00:19:20,425 --> 00:19:23,729
Also, the same applies
to Poong and Chef Eun-yeong.

526
00:19:23,795 --> 00:19:26,265
All you have to do is pick the order.

527
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:28,901
Which order will you take?

528
00:19:28,967 --> 00:19:31,236
Poong just raised his hand.

529
00:19:31,303 --> 00:19:33,572
I'll go to the place where I belong.

530
00:19:33,639 --> 00:19:36,275
I'll take the cooking comics round.

531
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,877
Naturally, I'll go with him.

532
00:19:38,944 --> 00:19:40,245
You're his natural enemy.

533
00:19:40,312 --> 00:19:43,182
She has never lost once against Poong.

534
00:19:43,248 --> 00:19:44,183
She's that good.

535
00:19:44,249 --> 00:19:46,084
Now, Poong and Eun-yeong are set.

536
00:19:46,151 --> 00:19:48,854
Naturally, the team round is also set,

537
00:19:48,921 --> 00:19:51,190
a dish that'll go well with lemonade.

538
00:19:51,256 --> 00:19:52,925
Chef Seon-yeop, are you pleased with this?

539
00:19:52,991 --> 00:19:55,327
Will he make less of a mess
for you to clean up?

540
00:19:55,394 --> 00:19:57,062
I'll have to keep an eye on him.

541
00:19:57,429 --> 00:19:59,531
YOU TOO, SEON-YEOP?

542
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:01,466
Do you like this order, Jong-won?

543
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:03,702
Two people don't necessarily mean
it's twice as efficient.

544
00:20:03,769 --> 00:20:05,737
It can go up by three to four times,

545
00:20:05,804 --> 00:20:07,239
so we'll do a good job together.

546
00:20:07,306 --> 00:20:08,674
WE'LL SHOW YOU A GREAT ROUND

547
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:10,175
I'll truly do my best.

548
00:20:10,242 --> 00:20:11,610
WITH ALL OF HIS HEART!

549
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:12,978
BEFORE THE HISTORICAL TEAM ROUND…

550
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:17,316
Then let us begin the round between
Webtoon Artist Poong and Chef Eun-yeong!

551
00:20:17,382 --> 00:20:20,319
THE COOK-OFF BEGINS NOW

552
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:24,489
<i>This is the first cook-off</i>
<i>using KARINA's ingredients.</i>

553
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:27,926
A woman who woke up
and found herself in comedy comics,

554
00:20:27,993 --> 00:20:29,194
Chef Park Eun-yeong,

555
00:20:29,261 --> 00:20:32,631
versus a man who woke up
and found himself in bizarre comics,

556
00:20:32,698 --> 00:20:34,700
Webtoon Artist Kim Poong.

557
00:20:34,766 --> 00:20:36,835
I have a feeling
that Poong has an advantage.

558
00:20:36,902 --> 00:20:39,605
-Probably.
-After all, he's a webtoon artist.

559
00:20:39,671 --> 00:20:41,006
He used to draw.

560
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:43,542
-Currently a chef.
-A TV personality who was an artist.

561
00:20:43,609 --> 00:20:46,912
When it comes to this, "I Woke Up
and Found Myself in Cooking Comics,"

562
00:20:46,979 --> 00:20:50,649
Poong has already made a few masterpieces.

563
00:20:50,716 --> 00:20:55,487
The infamous dung loach
has become his biggest work so far.

564
00:20:55,554 --> 00:20:56,655
In the past,

565
00:20:56,722 --> 00:21:00,259
-he has made the larva rice.
-The larva.

566
00:21:00,325 --> 00:21:02,127
They're like larvae on leaves!

567
00:21:02,194 --> 00:21:04,129
HAHAHAHAHAHA

568
00:21:04,796 --> 00:21:07,199
THIS WAS ALSO FOR THE ORDER,
"A DISH OUT OF A COMIC BOOK"

569
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,034
-We call it a piece of work.
-Of course.

570
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:10,969
-The larva rice.
-Is it really?

571
00:21:11,036 --> 00:21:13,505
Are you sure you'll be fine
with a bizarre looking dish?

572
00:21:13,572 --> 00:21:15,874
Actually, something like dung loach

573
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:17,509
was what I wanted to see today.

574
00:21:19,011 --> 00:21:21,280
Please make me a masterpiece.

575
00:21:21,346 --> 00:21:23,382
-I'm glad you're here.
-Wait.

576
00:21:23,448 --> 00:21:25,083
OH…

577
00:21:25,150 --> 00:21:27,886
We just got quite a scandalous transcript.

578
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,655
-What is it?
-It's from Eun-yeong.

579
00:21:29,721 --> 00:21:31,023
"I, Park Eun-yeong,

580
00:21:31,556 --> 00:21:33,859
am the KARINA of Chinese cuisine."

581
00:21:34,993 --> 00:21:35,994
You said this?

582
00:21:36,061 --> 00:21:37,162
-What?
-What?

583
00:21:37,229 --> 00:21:39,097
-When did you say this?
-Says who?

584
00:21:39,364 --> 00:21:41,566
I AM KARINA, I CAN'T BE TWO

585
00:21:41,633 --> 00:21:43,502
I didn't say that.

586
00:21:43,568 --> 00:21:46,772
That was a prevalent notion
in the world of Chinese cuisine.

587
00:21:46,838 --> 00:21:47,906
I didn't say it myself.

588
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:50,242
-Who said that?
-I've never heard it.

589
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:53,278
Poong, you've set a foot
into the world of Chinese cuisine,

590
00:21:53,345 --> 00:21:54,746
so have you heard this?

591
00:21:54,813 --> 00:21:56,581
I've never heard it in my life.

592
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:59,651
That's why I say you are
a bootleg Chinese chef from the streets.

593
00:21:59,718 --> 00:22:02,487
This kind of hearsay
does not reach the streets.

594
00:22:02,554 --> 00:22:05,257
Only those who are
authentically in the field have heard it.

595
00:22:05,324 --> 00:22:07,192
You'll get lots of awful DMs today.

596
00:22:07,259 --> 00:22:08,827
So non-Chinese chefs can't hear it?

597
00:22:08,894 --> 00:22:12,931
Then let's ask Witch With a Wok,
who's in the field. Have you heard it?

598
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:14,566
-I've heard it.
-Really?

599
00:22:14,633 --> 00:22:17,669
-Really?
-So Eun-yeong is the KARINA in her field?

600
00:22:17,736 --> 00:22:20,639
-So authentic chefs have heard it.
-Yes, only us.

601
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:23,875
-Why?
-What?

602
00:22:23,942 --> 00:22:26,178
-I've heard this too.
-You have?

603
00:22:26,244 --> 00:22:28,780
-You have?
-But I think she misheard it.

604
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:30,349
Someone who was walking by

605
00:22:30,415 --> 00:22:31,983
wanted a bottle of beer from her,

606
00:22:32,050 --> 00:22:34,619
so they said,
"Do you have a bottle of Corona?"

607
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:36,521
-Corona?
-No, it's not like that.

608
00:22:36,588 --> 00:22:38,957
-I think you misheard it.
-Listen to this guy.

609
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,692
He's getting ambitious.

610
00:22:40,759 --> 00:22:42,828
Not Corona, but KARINA, right?

611
00:22:42,894 --> 00:22:44,529
Yes, you're right. It's not Corona.

612
00:22:44,596 --> 00:22:45,864
KARINA of Chinese cuisine.

613
00:22:45,931 --> 00:22:48,934
Again, whoever wins the cook-off

614
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:53,205
will get the <i>Chef & My Fridge</i> tableware
as a prize.

615
00:22:53,271 --> 00:22:54,840
I want it too.

616
00:22:54,906 --> 00:22:56,208
I have to get it.

617
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,243
CHEF EUN-YEONG'S INGREDIENTS:

618
00:22:58,310 --> 00:23:01,213
PORK BELLY, PORK SHOULDER,
POTATO, RADISH, JJAJANG RAMYEON SOUP BASE

619
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:03,782
What are you making, Chef Eun-yeong?

620
00:23:03,849 --> 00:23:06,952
I'm making ArmagePork
with her favorite ingredient,

621
00:23:07,018 --> 00:23:08,987
pork belly.

622
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,422
It's a <i>jjajang</i> fried rice dish.

623
00:23:10,489 --> 00:23:12,424
-My gosh.
-I'll make <i>jjajang</i> fried rice

624
00:23:12,491 --> 00:23:15,627
and stack it up like a tree
as if it's from a comic book.

625
00:23:15,694 --> 00:23:17,229
-As you all know…
-<i>Jjajang</i> tree?

626
00:23:17,295 --> 00:23:20,165
…KARINA is famous
as the icy-looking AI-like beauty,

627
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:22,200
but I believe she's very warm-hearted.

628
00:23:22,267 --> 00:23:24,803
So on the outside,
it'll look like a pretty tree,

629
00:23:24,870 --> 00:23:26,238
but once you cut it in half,

630
00:23:26,304 --> 00:23:29,307
you'll see the dark rice inside.

631
00:23:29,374 --> 00:23:33,478
I wanted to express
the beautiful twist that KARINA has.

632
00:23:33,545 --> 00:23:35,113
It sounds like a dish from comics.

633
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,681
Different inside and out.

634
00:23:37,616 --> 00:23:39,885
KIM POONG'S INGREDIENTS: PORK NECK,
SHRIMP, BEECH MUSHROOM, SWEET PUMPKIN

635
00:23:39,951 --> 00:23:41,686
SPINACH, KIMCHI, RICE PAPER,
BALSAMIC SAUCE, OYSTER SAUCE

636
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:44,489
Up against Eun-yeong is Poong.
What are you making?

637
00:23:44,556 --> 00:23:46,558
The name of my dish is

638
00:23:47,125 --> 00:23:48,560
Karinasaur.

639
00:23:51,263 --> 00:23:53,198
Are you talking about her nickname?

640
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:55,500
I'll make a Karinasaur,

641
00:23:56,234 --> 00:23:59,771
which will look like
it came right out of a comic book.

642
00:23:59,838 --> 00:24:00,906
Like a Pikachu cutlet?

643
00:24:00,972 --> 00:24:03,074
Is he making me a dinosaur?

644
00:24:03,141 --> 00:24:04,876
So how will you make that dish?

645
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:07,846
Well… I'll make it edible, so don't worry.

646
00:24:07,913 --> 00:24:10,081
-Don't worry about it.
-No words needed.

647
00:24:10,582 --> 00:24:12,083
DID I JUST HEAR THAT RIGHT?

648
00:24:12,150 --> 00:24:14,119
You said you wanted it to be funny

649
00:24:14,186 --> 00:24:16,121
and somehow edible, right?

650
00:24:16,188 --> 00:24:18,590
THIS IS SO SCARY…

651
00:24:18,657 --> 00:24:21,259
So don't worry about anything

652
00:24:21,827 --> 00:24:25,330
and just put your focus on how it looks.

653
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:27,265
-We'll see when it's ready.
-Sure.

654
00:24:27,332 --> 00:24:31,603
This time, WINTER will join me
for the five-minute check.

655
00:24:31,670 --> 00:24:32,604
All right.

656
00:24:32,671 --> 00:24:34,005
And now,

657
00:24:34,072 --> 00:24:38,743
let us begin the round, "I Woke Up
and Found Myself in Cooking Comics."

658
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:42,280
"My twin sister was actually KARINA."

659
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:46,451
Self-claimed KARINA of Chinese cuisine,
Chef Park Eun-yeong.

660
00:24:46,518 --> 00:24:47,986
I can't believe this nonsense.

661
00:24:48,053 --> 00:24:49,521
-You can't believe it?
-Seriously.

662
00:24:49,588 --> 00:24:53,091
Here to send KARINA to Jurassic Park,

663
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:56,094
The Steven Poongpielberg of the show,

664
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:58,396
Webtoon Artist Kim Poong.

665
00:24:58,463 --> 00:25:02,501
Will they capture KARINA's heart
with dishes right out of a comic book?

666
00:25:02,567 --> 00:25:05,704
Let the 15-minute cook-off begin!

667
00:25:07,372 --> 00:25:09,140
It's all about the visuals.

668
00:25:09,608 --> 00:25:12,244
INTO THE WORLD OF COMICS!

669
00:25:12,310 --> 00:25:13,912
It's all about the visuals.

670
00:25:13,979 --> 00:25:17,182
Can you peel this?
But just the green part.

671
00:25:17,249 --> 00:25:19,684
-He gives him a job so smoothly.
-Seriously.

672
00:25:19,751 --> 00:25:22,187
-Are you acting as his kitchen toolman?
-Sure.

673
00:25:22,254 --> 00:25:24,823
-You have to peel that?
-Yes.

674
00:25:24,890 --> 00:25:26,324
He needs just the green part.

675
00:25:26,391 --> 00:25:29,060
It needs to look so good
that it captures our viewers too.

676
00:25:29,461 --> 00:25:30,295
ONION

677
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:31,396
What's he going to make?

678
00:25:31,463 --> 00:25:34,699
How's he going to make a dinosaur?

679
00:25:34,766 --> 00:25:35,834
I don't have enough time.

680
00:25:35,901 --> 00:25:38,670
Chili peppers, garlic, onion, and pork.

681
00:25:39,571 --> 00:25:41,373
Pork and shrimp. He'll grind everything.

682
00:25:41,606 --> 00:25:43,174
SOY SAUCE, OYSTER SAUCE, COOKING WINE

683
00:25:43,241 --> 00:25:46,344
-Didn't you put in too much?
-Isn't it way too full?

684
00:25:46,411 --> 00:25:48,079
What's he trying to do?

685
00:25:48,146 --> 00:25:50,582
-It's not working. It's an emergency.
-It won't even close.

686
00:25:50,649 --> 00:25:52,851
-He's nervous.
-It closed.

687
00:25:52,918 --> 00:25:54,853
-Oh, no.
-Will it work?

688
00:25:55,420 --> 00:25:57,622
-It's working.
-It's grinding.

689
00:25:58,456 --> 00:25:59,524
Karinasaur.

690
00:25:59,591 --> 00:26:00,425
Okay.

691
00:26:00,492 --> 00:26:02,494
Just a little bit of red pepper powder.

692
00:26:03,528 --> 00:26:05,130
The ground ingredients.

693
00:26:06,064 --> 00:26:08,166
-The dinosaur skin?
-The skin?

694
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:09,234
That's so scary.

695
00:26:09,301 --> 00:26:10,535
-It's scary.
-What's that?

696
00:26:10,602 --> 00:26:13,838
-It's the filling, like dumpling fillings.
-Dumplings.

697
00:26:13,905 --> 00:26:16,141
KARINA, between the taste
and how it looks,

698
00:26:16,207 --> 00:26:19,177
if one looks very shocking
but isn't as good, would you pick that?

699
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:21,546
If it's overwhelmingly shocking, I would.

700
00:26:21,613 --> 00:26:23,815
She's putting lots of focus
on how the dish looks.

701
00:26:23,882 --> 00:26:25,150
The visuals.

702
00:26:26,184 --> 00:26:28,787
This time, how it looks
is as important as how it tastes.

703
00:26:28,853 --> 00:26:30,989
-Potato.
-Potato.

704
00:26:31,056 --> 00:26:32,290
It's <i>jjajang</i>, so it needs that.

705
00:26:34,159 --> 00:26:35,393
Why does she need so much?

706
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:37,329
Will she cook it in the microwave?

707
00:26:37,395 --> 00:26:42,033
I'm sure most people have seen
what <i>jjajang</i> fried rice looks like.

708
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:44,736
But she mentioned a tree,
so we're looking forward to that.

709
00:26:45,303 --> 00:26:47,706
What's she trying to do?
It's hard to imagine.

710
00:26:48,139 --> 00:26:49,608
NEXT, RADISH SLICES

711
00:26:49,674 --> 00:26:51,509
She's making thin radish slices.

712
00:26:51,576 --> 00:26:53,578
-Radish?
-Radish and <i>jjajang</i> rice?

713
00:26:53,645 --> 00:26:55,981
-You're right.
-Will that become the tree?

714
00:26:56,047 --> 00:26:58,617
-How will she make a tree?
-Radish pickles?

715
00:26:58,683 --> 00:27:01,586
Maybe she'll cover the outside
with those slices.

716
00:27:01,653 --> 00:27:04,556
Sung-jun, can you cut these out
with those cookie cutters?

717
00:27:04,623 --> 00:27:06,691
-More bigger pieces than small ones.
-Yes, ma'am.

718
00:27:07,592 --> 00:27:08,827
Wait, she's older?

719
00:27:09,260 --> 00:27:10,895
GETTING CHILLS

720
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:11,963
Much older.

721
00:27:12,030 --> 00:27:16,234
-You're all making others do lots of work.
-They don't even hesitate.

722
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:20,038
-Sung-jun and Sam are helping.
-I want to see her cook, though.

723
00:27:20,105 --> 00:27:21,539
And some green onion.

724
00:27:22,907 --> 00:27:25,977
CHOP CHOP CHOP CHOP!

725
00:27:26,044 --> 00:27:27,812
You'll hurt your hand! Slow down!

726
00:27:27,879 --> 00:27:29,481
NOT AS PRECISE AS THE SOUND…

727
00:27:29,547 --> 00:27:30,849
He'll make a dinosaur shape

728
00:27:30,915 --> 00:27:32,751
-and fill it with that.
-The filling.

729
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:35,654
-I wonder how he'll make the dinosaur.
-Right?

730
00:27:35,720 --> 00:27:37,956
It's probably like a dim sum.

731
00:27:38,023 --> 00:27:38,957
T-Rex dim sum.

732
00:27:39,257 --> 00:27:41,426
ONE AT A TIME

733
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:43,461
Sung-jun, you need to hurry. I need lots.

734
00:27:43,528 --> 00:27:44,763
Wait.

735
00:27:46,598 --> 00:27:47,632
It's an emergency.

736
00:27:47,699 --> 00:27:50,301
LEARNED THE "WAIT" MOVE FROM HIS MASTER

