-At the end.

2179
01:23:07,182 --> 01:23:11,219
I called it <i>hwachae</i>,
but it's filled with lemonade inside,

2180
01:23:11,286 --> 01:23:13,388
along with fruit that you love.

2181
01:23:13,455 --> 01:23:14,556
-Inside?
-In there?

2182
01:23:16,091 --> 01:23:17,459
COLORFUL

2183
01:23:17,525 --> 01:23:19,627
-These are so…
-My gosh.

2184
01:23:19,694 --> 01:23:21,396
-I saw him scooping stuff up.
-Right?

2185
01:23:21,463 --> 01:23:24,332
-Melon and… Mango.
-Melon and probably mango.

2186
01:23:24,399 --> 01:23:26,835
-It's so pretty.
-That's what he was doing.

2187
01:23:27,802 --> 01:23:30,505
WHAT'S THE LEMONADE HWACHAE LIKE?

2188
01:23:30,572 --> 01:23:31,506
It must be refreshing.

2189
01:23:32,674 --> 01:23:35,143
They know how to capture her heart.

2190
01:23:35,543 --> 01:23:37,412
IT MUST BE GOOD

2191
01:23:37,479 --> 01:23:38,747
Wow.

2192
01:23:38,813 --> 01:23:39,881
ANOTHER BITE

2193
01:23:39,948 --> 01:23:42,317
-She'd love it.
-She has to.

2194
01:23:42,384 --> 01:23:43,752
Wow.

2195
01:23:44,452 --> 01:23:47,288
It's by far one of the best <i>hwachae</i>
I have ever had.

2196
01:23:47,355 --> 01:23:49,858
-One of the best?
-It's that good?

2197
01:23:49,924 --> 01:23:52,761
It just refreshed me
from everything I just had.

2198
01:23:52,994 --> 01:23:53,995
FEELS PROUD

2199
01:23:54,062 --> 01:23:54,996
It's good.

2200
01:23:55,063 --> 01:23:56,498
-Do you have some for WINTER?
-Sure.

2201
01:23:56,564 --> 01:23:58,800
Please share some with her.

2202
01:23:59,100 --> 01:24:00,301
PULLING OUT

2203
01:24:01,302 --> 01:24:02,604
Min-jeong.

2204
01:24:02,837 --> 01:24:04,339
SMILING LIKE HE'S THEIR DAD

2205
01:24:04,406 --> 01:24:05,740
Act like you're eating it.

2206
01:24:07,075 --> 01:24:09,444
-Like that.
-Act like it.

2207
01:24:09,511 --> 01:24:11,479
Pretend like
you're drinking from the straw.

2208
01:24:11,846 --> 01:24:13,681
OOH

2209
01:24:14,282 --> 01:24:15,216
Done.

2210
01:24:16,117 --> 01:24:18,553
WAS AT CHEF & MY FRIDGE

2211
01:24:18,620 --> 01:24:22,490
WINTER, please try
Hyun-suk and Seon-yeop's dishes first.

2212
01:24:22,557 --> 01:24:23,992
Lobster.

2213
01:24:24,059 --> 01:24:25,260
LOBSTER SHRIMP FIRST

2214
01:24:25,326 --> 01:24:27,429
Lobster made with shrimp?

2215
01:24:27,495 --> 01:24:28,963
YUM

2216
01:24:30,665 --> 01:24:32,167
-Mmm?
-Doesn't it taste like lobster?

2217
01:24:32,233 --> 01:24:34,536
-It's really like lobster.
-It is?

2218
01:24:34,602 --> 01:24:36,504
Really?

2219
01:24:36,571 --> 01:24:38,506
It really is,

2220
01:24:38,573 --> 01:24:39,908
and it's sour.

2221
01:24:39,974 --> 01:24:42,343
-It must be the hollandaise.
-Must be the sauce.

2222
01:24:42,410 --> 01:24:45,680
Next, steak with watermelon.

2223
01:24:45,747 --> 01:24:47,582
Those chefs are proud of their steaks.

2224
01:24:47,649 --> 01:24:48,483
Isn't it good?

2225
01:24:49,317 --> 01:24:54,022
EXCHANGING SIGNALS AGAIN

2226
01:24:54,556 --> 01:24:55,990
So you have to eat them together?

2227
01:24:56,057 --> 01:24:57,792
-Yes.
-I see.

2228
01:24:57,859 --> 01:25:00,862
-At once.
-I can make this at home. It's not hard.

2229
01:25:00,929 --> 01:25:03,598
-The watermelon?
-I can just cook it with steak.

2230
01:25:03,665 --> 01:25:06,835
It must be different in some way.

2231
01:25:06,901 --> 01:25:09,804
-She finished it all.
-She's done.

2232
01:25:09,871 --> 01:25:11,005
She must've waited a while.

2233
01:25:13,208 --> 01:25:16,044
I can't press
two buttons at the same time, can I?

2234
01:25:16,111 --> 01:25:18,046
-You have to choose just one.
-That's shrimp.

2235
01:25:18,113 --> 01:25:21,816
-Now, Chef Jong-won's dishes.
-Chef Jong-won's dishes.

2236
01:25:21,883 --> 01:25:24,085
-The shrimp.
-That's shrimp.

2237
01:25:24,152 --> 01:25:27,322
A HUGE SMILE

2238
01:25:27,889 --> 01:25:30,258
I get why she called this shrimp.

2239
01:25:30,325 --> 01:25:34,996
It does taste different
from that lobster shrimp.

2240
01:25:35,063 --> 01:25:38,900
That sauce is made with langoustine,
something more exclusive than lobster.

2241
01:25:39,167 --> 01:25:40,401
EMBARRASSED

2242
01:25:40,468 --> 01:25:42,670
-He feels anxious.
-Anyway, you had it

2243
01:25:42,737 --> 01:25:46,341
in your fridge, and you were
the first one who had this can.

2244
01:25:46,407 --> 01:25:49,010
-Next, the steak.
-That's a great mix too.

2245
01:25:49,077 --> 01:25:51,346
-It's tenderloin.
-Tenderloin steak.

2246
01:25:51,412 --> 01:25:55,150
They can compare directly
because you both made steak.

2247
01:25:55,216 --> 01:25:58,119
Unlike Chef Hyun-suk's steak,

2248
01:25:58,186 --> 01:25:59,521
it has many different flavors.

2249
01:26:01,122 --> 01:26:03,391
-There are lots of aromas too.
-Aromas.

2250
01:26:03,458 --> 01:26:05,460
-Ground pepper.
-Lemon zest.

2251
01:26:05,527 --> 01:26:08,596
It feels richer.

2252
01:26:08,663 --> 01:26:10,165
But that one…

2253
01:26:10,231 --> 01:26:11,866
Tasted poor?

2254
01:26:11,933 --> 01:26:14,335
Did it taste poor?

2255
01:26:14,802 --> 01:26:17,472
IT'S A MISUNDERSTANDING, GRANDPA

2256
01:26:17,539 --> 01:26:20,275
-I wouldn't be able to choose.
-No?

2257
01:26:20,341 --> 01:26:21,943
I'd try to push both at once.

2258
01:26:22,010 --> 01:26:24,679
-She just said that.
-I asked, "Can I press both at once?"

2259
01:26:24,746 --> 01:26:25,847
Can you just press both?

2260
01:26:25,914 --> 01:26:28,116
You're not allowed to do that.

2261
01:26:28,183 --> 01:26:30,518
Not a single person left without choosing.

2262
01:26:30,585 --> 01:26:31,753
Are you serious?

2263
01:26:31,819 --> 01:26:32,820
Not even once.

2264
01:26:32,887 --> 01:26:34,889
The one you choose will take the star.

2265
01:26:34,956 --> 01:26:37,392
Press one for Jong-won and Do-hee,

2266
01:26:37,458 --> 01:26:40,195
and two for Hyun-suk and Seon-yeop.

2267
01:26:40,261 --> 01:26:44,566
-Which leader will get to save his face?
-After all, they both tried hard.

2268
01:26:45,833 --> 01:26:47,335
Please stop.

2269
01:26:48,403 --> 01:26:49,237
You keep saying…

2270
01:26:49,304 --> 01:26:50,471
Make your decision.

2271
01:26:51,206 --> 01:26:53,274
-It must be heartbreaking.
-You're right.

2272
01:26:53,341 --> 01:26:54,442
It's hard to choose.

2273
01:26:54,509 --> 01:26:55,643
It's about your personal preference.

2274
01:26:55,710 --> 01:26:57,011
Make your decision.

2275
01:26:58,179 --> 01:27:01,082
I'll focus solely on the order
to make the decision.

2276
01:27:01,149 --> 01:27:03,418
-Solely on the order?
-The order?

2277
01:27:04,485 --> 01:27:05,720
-Okay.
-Did you press one?

2278
01:27:06,287 --> 01:27:07,255
I couldn't do that.

2279
01:27:07,322 --> 01:27:08,756
-She chose one.
-She did?

2280
01:27:08,823 --> 01:27:11,526
-She did.
-Oh, gosh! I want to cut my fingers off.

2281
01:27:11,593 --> 01:27:12,927
-All right.
-What now?

2282
01:27:12,994 --> 01:27:14,462
Let's find out!

2283
01:27:14,529 --> 01:27:15,830
KARINA's choice.

2284
01:27:15,897 --> 01:27:19,133
-I can't watch this.
-I'm going home.

2285
01:27:19,200 --> 01:27:20,702
Their release, "LEMONADE" was a hit.

2286
01:27:20,768 --> 01:27:23,705
So which set of dishes
went better with lemonade?

2287
01:27:23,771 --> 01:27:26,107
Is it Hyun-suk and Seon-yeop?

2288
01:27:26,174 --> 01:27:28,409
Or is it Jong-won and Do-hee?

2289
01:27:28,476 --> 01:27:31,546
-Not a single person has made a mistake.
-I'm nervous too.

2290
01:27:31,613 --> 01:27:32,747
This is awful.

2291
01:27:32,814 --> 01:27:34,616
I want to cut off my fingers.

2292
01:27:34,682 --> 01:27:35,783
I can't watch this.

2293
01:27:35,850 --> 01:27:38,853
Which one did KARINA choose?

2294
01:27:38,920 --> 01:27:39,754
Gosh.

2295
01:27:39,821 --> 01:27:43,258
The "LEMONADE" round. Was it Choi-Seon?

2296
01:27:43,324 --> 01:27:45,460
Or was it Lemon?

2297
01:27:46,261 --> 01:27:47,195
Who did she choose?

2298
01:27:50,598 --> 01:27:51,599
Who did she choose?

2299
01:27:51,833 --> 01:27:53,901
CHOI HYUN-SUK AND KIM SEON-YEOP WIN

2300
01:27:54,269 --> 01:27:56,771
HYUN-SUK AND SEON-YEOP'S
KARINA, THIS IS CHOI-SEON'S BEST WINS

2301
01:27:56,838 --> 01:27:58,439
Hyun-suk and Seon-yeop!

2302
01:28:00,375 --> 01:28:05,246
EVERYONE DID THEIR BEST
REGARDLESS OF THE RESULT

2303
01:28:07,315 --> 01:28:10,718
-Why did you choose them?
-I chose them because…

2304
01:28:10,785 --> 01:28:14,055
Well, when I had my first bite,

2305
01:28:14,122 --> 01:28:19,460
Chef Son's dishes had
many more wow factors.

2306
01:28:19,527 --> 01:28:23,464
But the dishes
that went much better with lemonade

2307
01:28:23,531 --> 01:28:26,167
were Chef Hyun-suk's.

2308
01:28:26,234 --> 01:28:29,971
It made me want to go
back and forth between the dishes.

2309
01:28:30,038 --> 01:28:33,374
-So it was how they paired.
-How they paired.

2310
01:28:33,441 --> 01:28:36,177
She wanted to have it with the meal
instead of having it as dessert.

2311
01:28:37,045 --> 01:28:38,479
Nothing beats the original cast.

2312
01:28:38,780 --> 01:28:40,915
CAN'T HIDE HIS SMILE

2313
01:28:40,982 --> 01:28:42,817
Look at his face.

2314
01:28:42,884 --> 01:28:45,853
-He can't hide how he feels.
-My gosh.

2315
01:28:45,920 --> 01:28:47,755
Fourteen years is hard to beat.

2316
01:28:47,822 --> 01:28:49,791
Let's hear from Chef Seon-yeop too.

2317
01:28:49,857 --> 01:28:52,260
I should've done my best to assist him,

2318
01:28:52,327 --> 01:28:56,864
but I ended up receiving his help.

2319
01:28:56,931 --> 01:29:01,169
Thank you very much
for giving me this great memory.

2320
01:29:01,969 --> 01:29:03,171
Don't say that.

2321
01:29:03,237 --> 01:29:05,406
I'm only here
as your supporter, Seon-yeop.

2322
01:29:05,473 --> 01:29:08,109
It must be a bummer, Jong-won.
Any thoughts?

2323
01:29:08,176 --> 01:29:10,244
I'm very happy for this team round

2324
01:29:10,311 --> 01:29:12,880
that I got to experience
with Do-hee and Seon-yeop.

2325
01:29:12,947 --> 01:29:16,050
The reason why Chef Hyun-suk
and I could be loved this much

2326
01:29:16,117 --> 01:29:17,518
is all thanks to our teams

2327
01:29:17,585 --> 01:29:19,921
who stay by our side
and work quietly with us.

2328
01:29:19,987 --> 01:29:24,025
So it was quite meaningful
that I got to cook with my teammate.

2329
01:29:24,092 --> 01:29:26,661
-Yes, and we witnessed it together.
-We did.

2330
01:29:26,728 --> 01:29:30,565
Please put the stars
on Team Hyun-suk, KARINA!

2331
01:29:31,332 --> 01:29:32,600
Great job.

2332
01:29:32,667 --> 01:29:35,570
GREAT JOB, EVERYONE

2333
01:29:35,970 --> 01:29:38,005
Put them on, KARINA.

2334
01:29:38,072 --> 01:29:41,142
Hyun-suk takes his seventh star!

2335
01:29:41,909 --> 01:29:43,378
Congratulations.

2336
01:29:43,444 --> 01:29:46,614
Also, the tableware set.

2337
01:29:46,681 --> 01:29:48,649
COMING UP: PREVIEW FOR
CHANG HANG-JUN & J.Y. PARK'S EPISODE

2338
01:29:48,716 --> 01:29:50,151
Congratulations!

2339
01:29:50,752 --> 01:29:52,453
Today's fridge owners are

2340
01:29:52,520 --> 01:29:54,622
Chang Hang-jun and J.Y. Park!

2341
01:29:54,689 --> 01:29:56,591
A world-renowned Korean cinematic legend,

2342
01:29:56,657 --> 01:29:58,226
-Chang Hang-jun.
-Sure.

2343
01:29:58,292 --> 01:29:59,227
JYP

2344
01:29:59,293 --> 01:30:00,595
is here!

2345
01:30:00,828 --> 01:30:01,929
THE TWO LEGENDS MEET

2346
01:30:01,996 --> 01:30:03,965
He's the happiest filmmaker right now.

2347
01:30:04,031 --> 01:30:05,433
It kind of feels like

2348
01:30:05,500 --> 01:30:08,970
a huge act of collective mockery.

2349
01:30:09,036 --> 01:30:10,605
He had a favor to ask you.

2350
01:30:10,671 --> 01:30:13,007
I, J.Y. Park, am a good actor.

2351
01:30:13,074 --> 01:30:14,475
I'm built for comedy.

2352
01:30:15,343 --> 01:30:17,612
Who could you have played
in <i>The King's Warden</i>?

2353
01:30:17,678 --> 01:30:19,113
Yoo Hai-jin's role.

2354
01:30:19,180 --> 01:30:21,315
J.Y. Park:
"I can act as well as Yoo Hai-jin."

2355
01:30:21,549 --> 01:30:22,750
THE LEGENDS GO BACK AND FORTH

2356
01:30:22,817 --> 01:30:23,785
THE FOODIES OF THE SHOW

2357
01:30:23,851 --> 01:30:24,786
WILL COOK FOR HANG-JUN

2358
01:30:24,852 --> 01:30:25,953
That's one too many tomatoes.

2359
01:30:26,020 --> 01:30:27,321
He's cooking his portion too.

2360
01:30:27,388 --> 01:30:28,589
Is that for one person?

2361
01:30:28,990 --> 01:30:30,591
MOUTH-WATERING VISUALS

2362
01:30:30,658 --> 01:30:32,059
That smells so good!

2363
01:30:32,293 --> 01:30:34,495
CHINESE VS. WESTERN CUISINE
A CLASH OF PRIDE

2364
01:30:34,562 --> 01:30:36,831
We'll take down those lousy Western chefs.

2365
01:30:36,898 --> 01:30:38,332
We'll beat the Chinese nobodies.

2366
01:30:38,399 --> 01:30:39,667
FIERCE MIND GAMES

2367
01:30:39,734 --> 01:30:41,068
Give them a good beating!

2368
01:30:41,369 --> 01:30:42,703
WHAT WAS THAT?

2369
01:30:43,070 --> 01:30:44,705
THE LUNACY OF THE CHINESE SISTER CHEFS

2370
01:30:45,139 --> 01:30:47,275
CLEANSING WITH SALT

2371
01:30:47,341 --> 01:30:48,276
GLANCES

2372
01:30:48,609 --> 01:30:49,610
GLANCES THE 2ND TIME

2373
01:30:49,677 --> 01:30:51,045
Why are you so cautious?

2374
01:30:51,112 --> 01:30:53,514
THE NOVICE LEGEND
STILL FINDS ATTENTION AWKWARD?

2375
01:30:59,921 --> 01:31:02,890
Don't be so cautious.
You've surpassed ten million admissions.

2376
01:31:12,600 --> 01:31:17,371
Subtitle translation by: Eunsook Youn
